cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on Polaris, please cite it as below."
title: "Polaris: a post-quantum, zero-knowledge, compulsion-resistant national identity-token reference implementation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khaklin
    given-names: Egor
version: "9.304"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EgorKhaklin/polaris-id"
url: "https://egorkhaklin.github.io/polaris-id/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - digital identity
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - ML-DSA
  - anti-coercion
abstract: >-
  A working reference implementation of a national identity-token system whose
  guarantees are enforced in the database schema: post-quantum signatures
  (ML-DSA-65), zero-knowledge verification with an independent second witness,
  an append-only audit of record, and duress-resistant operation. Educational;
  notional data only.
